of 29 the same inode. The back target was absent before the edge fill, so the shipped back art was
never written. The edge fill kept its source at `5411e37e...` and wrote `881e93b2...`. The prepared
teacher front holds `09014118...`.

STEP 2 ran one build with `--top hlogo` in one heavy-run wrapper. It exits 0 on the first attempt. It
prints `Covers of Level 2 Unit 1 set 1: 32 pages, 44 files` and 4 lines `All checks pass.`.

STEP 3 copied 34 files as byte copies into the 2 new folders `readers-a3/` and `readers-leaf/` of
`covers-quest-v1`. All 34 SHA-256 pairs are equal. The 4 book PNGs equal the shipped r2 files, and
the 4 book PDFs differ. Those 8 lines are information only.

STEP 4 ran 15 print-check lines: 14 PASS and 1 FAIL. `PRINT_GATE` exits 0 on both reader print files
with `All checks pass.` The `CHECK_4_TEXT_COUNTS_LEAF` line is FAIL: "Storytime Advantage" reads 0
times on 13 of the 14 leaf pages. The 2 diagnosis captures show the cause. The series box is 30 mm
wide at 9 pt, so the name wraps and the second word falls to the page edge.

STEP 5 made the 3 contact sheets. STEP 6 rewrote `MANIFEST.txt` with 85 lines, and its 48 old lines
are byte-equal.

STEP 7 inserted one plan sub-bullet under Task 2.9, and Task 2.9 stays `[~]`. The commit of the
scripts, the captures, and the plan is `69acdd26`. This log is the second commit.

The orchestrator accepted the C4 leaf finding. A new Red and Green pair fixes the leaf series line,
not this role.

